{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 46, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.2-3b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a film that delves into the complex and often tumultuous world of harvard university's warring rivalries, albeit one centered around the creation of facebook. directed by david finch erdman and released in 2010, this movie boasts a stellar cast, phenomenal performances, and a captivating narrative that will keep you hooked from start to finish.\n\nthe story revolves around mark zuckerberg, played by jesse eisenberg, a highly intelligent and socially awkward sophomore who creates a website called \"facemash\" that allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive. this catches the attention of erron musk, a business-savvy sophomore who convinces mark to expand his creation into a full-fledged social networking site.\n\nas facebook gains immense popularity, it attracts the attention of the numerous colleges and universities across the country. mark, accompanied by his friends and business partners, edward sutherland and andy mcnerney, must navigate the complex web of relationships, friendships, and rivalries within harvard's elite college scene.\n\none of the standout aspects of this film is its portrayal of the characters' mental states. mark, in particular, is depicted as a genius with a fragile ego, often oscillating between vulnerability and arrogance. jared leto's portrayal of sean parker, the initially enthusiastic partner who becomes increasingly disillusioned with mark's leadership, is equally impressive.\n\nthe cinematography and editing in the movie are also noteworthy, capturing the frenetic energy of harvard's campus life and the fast-paced world of social media. the film's score, composed by todd field, perfectly complements the mood and atmosphere, elevating the emotional impact of each scene.\n\nthe social network has been both praised and criticized for its depiction of mark zuckerberg and the early days of facebook. some have argued that the film portrays mark as a one-dimensional villain, while others see it as a nuanced portrayal of the complex individual behind thefacebook phenomenon. regardless, the film's attention to detail and commitment to accuracy make it a compelling and thought-provoking watch.\n\noverall, the social network is a gripping and insightful film that sheds light on the often-overlooked world of social media and the people behind it. with its stellar performances, captivating narrative, and phenomenal cinematography, this movie is a must-watch for anyone interested in the intersection of technology, social dynamics, and the human experience.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.20552276074886322}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.00035589560866355896}, {"token": " network", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.04680097848176956}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.0009609610424377024}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -2.0224790573120117}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.012613166123628616}, {"token": " del", "logprob": -0.6436415910720825}, {"token": "ves", "logprob": -7.748573807475623e-06}, {"token": " into", "logprob": -0.020764002576470375}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -1.0251946150674485e-05}, {"token": " complex", "logprob": -1.2828706502914429}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.09703605622053146}, {"token": " often", "logprob": -0.5377976298332214}, {"token": " tumult", "logprob": -0.3889788091182709}, {"token": "uous", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " world", "logprob": -0.24246883392333984}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " har", "logprob": -1.098036527633667}, {"token": "vard", "logprob": -0.0021064728498458862}, {"token": " university", "logprob": -0.18101739883422852}, {"token": "'s", "logprob": -0.1034860908985138}, {"token": " w", "logprob": -0.5919256210327148}, {"token": "arring", "logprob": -0.6691581606864929}, {"token": " rival",